<title>HONG KONG: HK Building &amp; Loan H1 net up 5.13 pct.</title>
<headline>HK Building &amp; Loan H1 net up 5.13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   10.0  vs 9.5 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    3.0   vs 3.0 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil   vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    22.47 vs 21.37</p>
<p>    Turnover		     50.52 vs 45.02</p>
<p>    Company name		 Hong Kong Building and Loan Agency</p>
<p>				     Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  October 15-18</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 31</p>
<p>NOTE - Hong Kong Building and Loan provides mortgages to middle income flat owner-occupiers.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings and interim dividend have been adjusted to take account of the bonus issue of two-for-one share and also the sub-division of shares of one-into-five shares both effected on June 25, 1996.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
